 ## Retries
 
-Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
-can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
-drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
+Each capture attempt sends a fresh idempotency key because the gateway sometimes rejects a retried capture with a
+"duplicate idempotency key" error. See [the capture implementation](../../larder/capture.py) for the retry policy.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The gateway can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024
+retries that drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice. Fresh keys reintroduce this risk; follow the
+[gateway timeout runbook](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md) to investigate timed-out captures.
 
